Description: Fix building the calculations C extension on Linux
 mspy/calculations is a mandatory C extension (mod_signal, mod_pattern,
 mod_formulator and plot_objects all import it directly with no
 fallback); upstream only ships a prebuilt Windows .pyd and the build
 script itself only works on Windows/Mac.
 .
 Two independent problems, both fixed here:
 .
 1. numpy 2.x reorganized its C headers. calculations.c does
    `#include "arrayobject.h"` (needs numpy's include/numpy directory
    itself on the include path) but arrayobject.h then does
    `#include "numpy/ndarrayobject.h"` (needs the parent of that
    directory on the path too). Upstream's setup.py only added the
    first, so nested numpy headers failed to resolve. Add both.
 2. PyArray_DOUBLE was fully removed from the numpy 2.x C API (it was
    a pre-1.7 alias); replace with its current name, NPY_DOUBLE.
 .
 Also drops a hardcoded personal Windows include path
 (C:\Xilinx\Vivado\...) that was never applicable outside upstream's
 own machine and produced an invalid-escape-sequence warning even on
 Windows.
Author: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/SCIENCE-OPEN/mmassx/pull/2
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
--- a/mspy/calculations.c
+++ b/mspy/calculations.c
@@ -1676,7 +1676,7 @@ PyArrayObject *array_md2py( m_arrayd *p_inarr )
     dim[1] = (npy_intp) p_inarr->cell;
     
     // make python array
-    p_outarr = (PyArrayObject *) PyArray_SimpleNew(nd, dim, PyArray_DOUBLE);
+    p_outarr = (PyArrayObject *) PyArray_SimpleNew(nd, dim, NPY_DOUBLE);
     if ( p_outarr == NULL ) {
         return NULL;
     }
--- a/mspy/setup.py
